id: pm-6sc8jq
title: "GH-891: external blockers make graph stale_lifecycle_block impossible to resolve truthfully"
description: GitHub issue #891 reports that pm graph audit treats blocked work without an open tracker predecessor as stale even when blocked_reason precisely documents a real external party or event that should not be fabricated as a PM item. The audit needs an honest first-class external-blocker policy or a blocked_reason-backed classification so machine governance remains actionable.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ux,"area:governance","area:graph",external-blocker,github-report,truthfulness
created_at: "2026-08-04T08:43:47.536Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T11:47:54.591Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#e5139491a52f7c630a58be71"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The SDK governance policy distinguishes missing blocker evidence from documented external blockers without inventing graph nodes; CLI, SDK, MCP, contracts, docs, and tests expose one deterministic externally-blocked representation and severity policy; The existing genuinely stale blocked case remains actionable and a negative control proves the audit still catches it"
parent: pm-6x7o
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: pm-cli 2026.8.3; external fleet tracker; pm graph audit --json
repro_steps: Create or inspect a blocked item with a precise non-empty blocked_reason and no internal ordering predecessor; run pm graph audit --json; observe stale_lifecycle_block with remediation that requires fabricating or reopening a tracker item
expected_result: Externally blocked work has a truthful machine-readable representation and does not emit an actionable stale-lifecycle defect when its evidence is complete
actual_result: The audit reports stale_lifecycle_block and recommends an internal edge or active status even when neither is truthful
customer_impact: "Agents learn to ignore graph audits or fabricate placeholder work, weakening governance and context truth"
